\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Theorem}
\title{Reflection positivity of the connection marginal}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The connection marginal of the
\vocabk{cellular paired functional}{fdip-00XQ} is a
reflection-positive probability law on the full connection
function algebra, with masses
##{\nu(U)=\begin{cases}
 525/2108,&u_0=u_1,\\
 529/2108,&u_0=-u_1.
 \end{cases}}
It is therefore reflection positive on any specified
connection half-subalgebra.}

\proof{
\p{Restricting the paired functional to a scalar function
of #{U} integrates the exterior weight to #{\det K_U}.
The values and their sum are \ref{fdip-00XW} and
\ref{fdip-00XX}. They are positive and sum to one. The
geometric reflection fixes each #{U} pointwise, so for any
connection function #{h},
##{B_\nu(h,h)=\sum_{U\in\Omega}\nu(U)
                          \overline{h(U)}h(U)\ge0.}
This is the claimed form on the whole algebra. Restriction
preserves the inequality.}
}

\p{The rank-one kernel component is
\leanref/tauceti{TauCeti.posSemidef_rankOne}.
Its use requires the pointwise-fixed reflection and the
computed nonnegative weights.}
